From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: thumbnails of videos and PDFs

Two more thumbnail providers beside the WIC one of 0153, registered as the
ShellEx {e357fccd-a995-4576-b01f-234630154e96} handler of their types in
wine.inf. Videos (.mp4 .m4v .mkv .webm .avi .wmv .mov .mpg .mpeg .ogv
.3gp): a frame from Media Foundation's source reader (winegstreamer
underneath) with video processing to RGB32, at a tenth of the length, or
three tenths if that frame is dark. The processor's stride from Wine is in
pixels, so a stride too small for a row keeps only its sign. PDFs: the first
page, rendered by sg-session's sg-pdf (poppler) -- run as
\\?\unix/usr/bin/sg-pdf --thumbnail PDF SIZE PNG (SG_PDF names another)
and read back through WIC; up to 20 s, or PNG.err on failure. The providers
take IInitializeWithItem / IInitializeWithFile (a path), not a stream.

Gate: test/explorer3-gate.sh.
